# Audi A8 D4 four-door saloon, 2010-2017.
#
# The third A8: the aluminium D4 body with the wide single-frame grille,
# the full-LED headlamps and the long-wheelbase option. The S8 and the
# W12 are variants on the same shell.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Audi_A8
#
# Dimensions 5.131 x 1.948 x 1.461 m, wheelbase 2.992 m.
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is a near broadside of a 2012 4.2 quattro; the
# front and rear three-quarters are the same car. Level is not verified.
#
# Colours: grade (d); no UK chart was established. Black, silver, grey and
# blue are plain names. Weights 9, 8, 7, 6, total 30, provisional.
#
# Speed 250 km/h. Comfort 105/337, on the line 180 + 1.5 x 105. Classes 3,4.
# Dates are road presence: 2010 intro, retires staggered 2034-2037.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/audi-a8-d4.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/audi-a8-d4.dae. References:
# citycars/references/audi-a8-d4/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: there is no door-shoulder scallop or wheel-arch flare,
# and the lamps are flat panels rather than sculpted units; the rear window is
# more upright than the photograph's. At 128 px the large single-frame grille,
# slim angular lamps and long low body read as a D4 A8.


obj=citycar
name=AudiA8D4(Black)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=9
intro_year=2010
intro_month=1
retire_year=2037
retire_month=6
speed=250
class=3,4
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=105
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=337

